# Provenance hashes raw file bytes (scripts/benchmark_provenance.py), so a file
# whose line endings depend on the machine can never verify across machines.
# Some recorded hashes were produced on Windows from CRLF working copies while
# the committed blobs are LF; those runs now match only after line-ending
# repair, which verification reports rather than hides. Normalising here stops
# new records from drifting the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.faiss binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
